      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Exercise: background subtraction over video - one foreach body, not N copies\n\nA fixed-camera pedestrian clip (LoadVideo -> Video Slice -> Get Video Components = an IMAGE batch).\nBACKGROUND PLATE (computed ONCE): 'CV Temporal Reduce' takes the MEDIAN of every pixel OVER TIME. Anything that moves occupies a pixel only a minority of the frames, so it averages out and the empty scene remains - the fixed-camera analog of AR detecting its marker once. The plate seeds the output batch.\nPER FRAME (Inspire foreach, one body): 'Image -> CV Array' -> 'CV Background Model (Update)' with mean = the plate and learning_rate 0 (a fixed-reference detector: a pixel is foreground when it sits more than 'threshold' standard deviations from the plate) -> 'Mask Grow/Shrink' (open) despeckles -> 'Overlay Masks' paints the foreground on the frame -> APPEND to the running batch ('Image Batch' = the fold accumulator). 'ForeachListEnd' yields the whole segmented batch -> 'Preview Image'.\n\ncv2's stateful BackgroundSubtractorMOG2/KNN are avoided on purpose: such a subtractor mutates itself on every frame, so it cannot travel along a link. When you do want one, 'CV Background Subtract (Batch)' runs a whole batch through it inside a single node (workflow 60)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
